[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Main Control APP

[SFMEA]
UID: SFMEA-FW-1
INITIAL_P: 3 - Probable
INITIAL_S: 4 - Critical
INITIAL_RI: 12/ Zone 2 ALAP
RESIDUAL_P: 1 - Improbable
RESIDUAL_S: 4 - Critical
RESIDUAL_RI: 4/ Zone 1 Acceptable
TITLE: State: Emission
FAILURE_MODE: >>>
FW does not transition to the termination state following a manual PC stop command.
<<<
FORESEEABLE_SEQUENCE_OF_EVENTS: >>>
1. During emission, user manually presses the "stop" command on the PC.
2. PC sends command to FW
3. No stop command is received by the FW
4. X-ray emission continues
<<<
EFFECT: >>>
Unwanted X-Ray exposure to the patient
<<<
CAUSES: >>>
1. Firmware Defect
<<<
RISK_CONTROLS: >>>
1. Mechanism - Backup timers
2. Mechanism - Emergency Stop buttons
3. Unit test + Code Review
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SW-H1FWMC-203
  ROLE: Refines

[SFMEA]
UID: SFMEA-FW-2
INITIAL_P: 3 - Probable
INITIAL_S: 4 - Critical
INITIAL_RI: 12/ Zone 2 ALAP
RESIDUAL_P: 1 - Improbable
RESIDUAL_S: 4 - Critical
RESIDUAL_RI: 4/ Zone 1 Acceptable
TITLE: Backup Timer Communication
FAILURE_MODE: >>>
FW does not receive data from the backup timers
<<<
FORESEEABLE_SEQUENCE_OF_EVENTS: >>>
1. Upon emission, the backup timers are signaled to begin
2. Timer does not respond
3. FW has no comparison for its master timer
4. X-Ray emission lasts for imprecise amount of time
<<<
EFFECT: >>>
X-Ray exposure happens for an unwanted amount of time.
<<<
CAUSES: >>>
1. Firmware Defect
2. Connection to timers is compromised
3. Backup Timer FW defect
<<<
RISK_CONTROLS: >>>
1. Mechanism - two backup timers.
2. Code solution - I2C monitors for NACK signal to report a fault
3. Code solution - FW throws fault with no communication
4. Unit test + Code Review
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SW-H1FWMC-179
  ROLE: Refines

[SFMEA]
UID: SFMEA-FW-3
INITIAL_P: 3 - Probable
INITIAL_S: 4 - Critical
INITIAL_RI: 12/ Zone 2 ALAP
RESIDUAL_P: 1 - Improbable
RESIDUAL_S: 4 - Critical
RESIDUAL_RI: 4/ Zone 1 Acceptable
TITLE: PC Ethernet Communication
FAILURE_MODE: >>>
FW does not receive data from the PC
<<<
FORESEEABLE_SEQUENCE_OF_EVENTS: >>>
1. The FW is operating in a given state
2. Communication between the FW and the PC is lost
3. State of operation cannot be changed by the user
4. Unwanted operation, including but not limited to X-Ray emission, continues as previously activated
<<<
EFFECT: >>>
Operation continues without ability to change through the GUI, such as X-Ray emission
<<<
CAUSES: >>>
1. FW Defect
2. UDP packet is lost
<<<
RISK_CONTROLS: >>>
1. Mechanism - Emergency Stops can stop the system entirely
2. Code solution - automatic sensing and onboard timers should automatically transition the state
3. Unit test + Code Review
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SW-H1FWMC-183
  ROLE: Refines

[SFMEA]
UID: SFMEA-FW-4
INITIAL_P: 3 - Probable
INITIAL_S: 4 - Critical
INITIAL_RI: 12/ Zone 2 ALAP
RESIDUAL_P: 1 - Improbable
RESIDUAL_S: 4 - Critical
RESIDUAL_RI: 4/ Zone 1 Acceptable
TITLE: External Watchdog
FAILURE_MODE: >>>
Firmware is caught in a function and the system does not react or respond
<<<
FORESEEABLE_SEQUENCE_OF_EVENTS: >>>
1. The FW is in normal operation and accesses a function
2. An interrupt or bug occurs
3. The FW cannot escape the function
4. Machine operation stalls
<<<
EFFECT: >>>
X-Ray emission continues without stopping
<<<
CAUSES: >>>
1. Firmware Defect
<<<
RISK_CONTROLS: >>>
1. Code solution - Watchdog triggers a reset if no refresh signal is sent from FW
2. Mechanism - Emergency Stops can stop emission
3. Unit test + Code Review
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SW-H1FWMC-299
  ROLE: Refines

[SFMEA]
UID: SFMEA-FW-5
INITIAL_P: 3 - Probable
