[[SECTION]]
TITLE: SFMEA Risk Prioritization

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
The Risk Index (RI) is a critical factor in prioritizing corrective actions. It provides a relative indication of the identified failure indicating whether the risk requires further mitigation or control.

RI is calculated as follows (see QSP-017 risk management, referenced in section 5):

RI = Probability of Occurrence (P) X Severity (S)

.. image:: _assets/risk_prioritization.jpeg
   :alt: Risk index matrix by occurrence rank and severity rank
   :width: 100%
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: SFMEA Risk Acceptability

[TEXT]
